QEC-ADA is an independent Ada/SPARK implementation project. Its initial native
GF(3) kernel, CLI and browser GUI are new work, not a mechanical source port.

Historical QEC research documentation has been copied without byte changes
from QSOLKCB/QEC, source commit 27bbc798c4e38138ca5b0fff70b15c3271a1917d, under docs/reference/qec/.
The files retain the licence and attribution applicable at the source. Original
Git blob SHA-1 values and exclusions are in fixtures/qec_reference_manifest.json.

QEC-ADA makes no representation that archived QEC experiments, third-party
packages, hardware measurements, or historical decoder capabilities have been
implemented, proved, or reproduced by this new project.

For QEC provenance, see docs/reference/qec/CITATION_AND_ATTRIBUTION.md and
the donor repository's LICENCE and NOTICE records. Where a cited historical
reference requires a source path, interpret it relative to the pinned QEC
commit, not the QEC-ADA repository root.

The fixed cyclic [[5,1,3]]_3 qutrit decoder is an independently written Ada
implementation of the mathematical model and bounded enumeration in QEC
src/qec/decoder/qutrit/{gf3,stabilizer,codes,exact}.py at
27bbc798c4e38138ca5b0fff70b15c3271a1917d, under MPL-2.0.

The precomputed one-site contributions and identity-site skipping adapt
the general mechanisms OPT-INV-001 and OPT-REDUCE-001 from QSOLKCB/OPT,
Apache-2.0. No OPT source is copied. There is no universal performance
claim. The new classical selector follows QEC Strowger's first-free
ordering concept but does not claim complete Strowger equivalence or receipts.
